# rotate-tick.env.local.example — operator env for the ROTATION TICK's launchd
# agent. Copy to rotate-tick.env.local (same dir; GITIGNORED — it carries
# machine-local paths and arming decisions), edit, then re-render + reload:
#
#     SWARM_HOME=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering bin/swarm-launchd-install.sh
#
# Every KEY=value line here is merged into com.qofi.swarm-rotate-tick.plist's
# EnvironmentVariables at render time (bin/swarm-launchd-install.sh — see its
# header for the format/validation rules). Values are taken LITERALLY: no shell
# quoting or expansion happens here; a "$1" in a value stays a literal "$1" for
# the consuming script's `sh -c` invocation to expand. The template owns
# SWARM_HOME / CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR / SWARM_STALE_SECONDS / SWARM_TMUX_BIN —
# re-declaring those here is a render error.
#
# THE ARMING MODEL. The committed template deliberately ships UNARMED: without
# SWARM_CREDSWAP_CMD the tick's actuator (swarm-rotate.sh) REFUSES a live swap.
# This file is the "operator adds it out-of-band" channel the template comment
# refers to. Delete the file and re-render to disarm (reverts byte-identical).

# ── CALIBRATION GATE (do NOT skip to live) ───────────────────────────────────
# 1 = render the tick with --observe: each tick LOGS burn-vs-budget + the real
# limit signal to ~/.config/swarm/rotate-tick.log and rotates NOTHING. Run the
# observe→calibrate→enable sequence (PROJECT_SPEC §10, "Rotation hardening")
# before flipping to 0. Consumed by the installer; never lands in the plist.
SWARM_TICK_OBSERVE=1

# ── THE ACTUATOR — pick ONE model ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# MODEL A (recommended): NO-RESTART IN-PLACE RE-AUTH (swarm-reauth.sh).
# On NEAR/AT the tick runs swarm-reauth.sh: /login fires in a DEDICATED isolated
# session (swarm-login-probe — never a CTO pane), the OAuth URL posts to the
# product Discord channel, the operator's browser picks the next account, and
# NOTHING restarts — running leads keep their in-RAM state. No checkpoint, no
# clean-boundary guard, no account ring (the browser chooses the account, so
# SWARM_ACCOUNTS / SWARM_CHECKPOINT_CMD / SWARM_CREDSWAP_CMD are all unused).
# Pair it with SWARM_TICK_ALERT_CMD below — the fail-loud net for a lead that
# does not adopt the fresh credential in place.
#SWARM_ROTATE_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-reauth.sh
#
# MODEL B (legacy): CHECKPOINT → CREDSWAP → FLEET RESTART (swarm-rotate.sh, the
# tick's default). Needs all four knobs below. The relay is wired BARE — NO "$1"
# suffix: its positional arg is a SWARM name, not an account handle; the account
# CHOICE happens in the operator's browser (the relay diagnoses the "$1"
# miswiring loudly). The ring handles are NOMINAL under the relay (ring math and
# logging only). Rotation = fleet restart = RAM-state loss, guarded by the
# clean-boundary rail.
#SWARM_CREDSWAP_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-login-relay.sh
#SWARM_ACCOUNTS=max-a max-b
#SWARM_CHECKPOINT_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-checkpoint.sh "$1"

# Rotation threshold (both models): NEAR fires when either window's used_pct >=
# this; AT at >= 100.
#SWARM_ROTATE_THRESHOLD_PCT=95

# ── THE STUCK-PANE SAFETY NET (Model A's fail-loud rail; standing) ───────────
# Runs every LIVE tick BEFORE routing (so it fires on OK verdicts too). If a CTO
# lead is PARKED on a cap banner while the account has HEADROOM, it did not pick
# up the rotated credential in place: post ONE deduped alert to the product
# channel naming the stuck lead(s). NEVER restarts anything. Suppressed when the
# poll verdict is AT/UNKNOWN (a park during a genuine cap is expected, not a
# stuck lead). Best-effort: a failure here never affects routing.
#SWARM_TICK_ALERT_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-reauth-verify.sh

# ── THE USAGE DETECTOR (/usage TUI scraper — AUTHORITATIVE) ──────────────────
# The poller's probe. It scrapes Anthropic's OWN percentages from the /usage
# panel (5h session + weekly windows). EXACT — no token budgets. Prefer it over
# the ccusage burn proxy, which mis-counts because CACHE READS don't count
# against the Max cap (proxy read weekly 97.5% while /usage read 6% on this
# fleet). It drives /usage in a DEDICATED, ISOLATED session (swarm-usage-probe)
# — a plain claude on the DEFAULT account, never bound to Discord, never a CTO
# pane — so it can NEVER interrupt a lead's coordination. The default account is
# the fleet's shared credential, so its /usage equals any default-account lead's.
# The session is created once and reused, recreated if unhealthy.
#SWARM_USAGE_PROBE=bash /path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-usage-adapter-tui.sh
# Tunables (optional): SWARM_USAGE_PROBE_SESSION (default swarm-usage-probe),
# SWARM_USAGE_PROBE_CWD (default $SWARM_HOME — must be a claude-TRUSTED dir),
# SWARM_USAGE_TUI_TIMEOUT (12), SWARM_USAGE_PROBE_LAUNCH_TIMEOUT (40).

# ── LEGACY: the ccusage burn PROXY (superseded — DO NOT rely on it) ──────────
# Kept for reference only. Needs token budgets AND mis-counts cache reads; use
# the /usage scraper above. launchd's minimal PATH has no ccusage/npx (npx also
# needs node), so it would need bunx: SWARM_CCUSAGE_CMD=/Users/<you>/.bun/bin/bunx ccusage
#SWARM_USAGE_PROBE=bash /path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-usage-adapter-ccusage.sh
#SWARM_5H_TOKEN_BUDGET=200000000
#SWARM_WEEKLY_TOKEN_BUDGET=2000000000

# ── REAL cap signal as the authoritative hard stop (MODEL B ONLY) ────────────
# swarm-limit-detect --or-poll emits AT immediately if any live pane shows a
# genuine cap-HIT banner, else delegates to the /usage poll (SWARM_USAGE_PROBE)
# and passes its OK/NEAR/AT through. The detector fires ONLY on cap-HIT phrasing
# ("...limit reached", "reached your usage limit", "rate limit exceeded", ...) —
# never on Claude Code's global allowance notice or the leads' own "rate limit"
# conversation. Tune via SWARM_LIMIT_PATTERNS / SWARM_LIMIT_EXCLUDE_PATTERNS.
#
# DO NOT wire this under MODEL A (no-restart). A lead that failed to adopt the
# fresh credential parks on a cap banner; with the banner as the trigger, that
# one stuck pane would re-fire the re-auth EVERY tick — an endless loop of login
# URLs none of which the stuck pane can use. Under Model A the percentage poll
# (account-level, reads the NEW account via the recycled probe) is the trigger,
# and the banner is an ALERT-only signal (SWARM_TICK_ALERT_CMD above).
#SWARM_POLL_CMD=/path/to/qofi-claude-engineering/bin/swarm-limit-detect.sh --or-poll

# ── OPTIONAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Escalation hook for ring exhaustion (every account capped).
#SWARM_ATTENTION_CMD=notify-ops "$1"
